---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site.ts';

const title = `About ${SITE.name} — a wishing well for AI builders`;
const description = `The story behind ${SITE.name}: a wishing and blessing platform for people bringing AI products into the world.`;
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <Breadcrumbs trail={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'About' }]} />
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>About {SITE.name}</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      {SITE.name} is a wishing and blessing platform for people building AI products. We gather thoughtful projects beneath
      one sky, then invite the community to help the launches they believe in shine a little brighter.
    </p>
  </div>

  <article class="prose">
    <h2>Why it is called that</h2>
    <p>
      The name comes from the moment before a launch: a mix of hope, nerves, and the courage to let an idea leave your hands.
      We want this to feel like a place that understands that moment. Each founder can share the intention behind their work,
      receive a blessing written for their product, and find encouragement from people who choose to light a star for it.
    </p>

    <h2>How projects find their place</h2>
    <p>
      We look across communities, research releases, product announcements, and official sources for projects worth knowing.
      That research helps us find candidates; it never publishes anything automatically. A human reads each candidate, and the entry text is
      written from scratch against what the product actually does. Regular maintenance keeps the collection useful and up to date.
    </p>

    <h2>What will never happen here</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Paid placement or a priority review fee. Every founder enters the same sky.</li>
      <li>Reciprocal-link requirements. The badge is optional and carries no weight either way.</li>
      <li>Auto-generated descriptions. A model helps us find things and draft long passages; nothing goes public that a person has not read and corrected.</li>
      <li>Mass ingestion. Every project receives thoughtful review before it appears.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Pricing pages lie, and this index is wrong about things sometimes. If an entry misstates what your product costs or does,
      email <a href={'mailto:' + SITE.email}>{SITE.email}</a> with a link to the source and it gets fixed in the next round —
      that is a genuine request, not a form reply.
    </p>

    <h2>Colophon</h2>
    <p>
      The wish sky grows through thoughtful review and community participation. Star votes are stored without account creation,
      and a browser can light one star for each wish. We write and maintain this place for people building ambitious things,
      with room for an idea at every stage of its journey.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
